# Terraform state contains the generated DB password and secret metadata.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform/

# .terraform.lock.hcl is deliberately tracked, not ignored. It pins the provider versions
# and their checksums, which is what makes an apply from CI resolve the same providers as an
# apply from a laptop. HashiCorp's own guidance is to commit it, and it holds no secret:
# versions and hashes only. Same reasoning as prisma's migration_lock.toml, un-ignored in
# Phase A of this migration for the same reason.

# Local var files (cron_secret is sensitive). The committed example is fine.
terraform.tfvars
*.auto.tfvars
!terraform.tfvars.example

# Crash logs / plans
crash.log
*.tfplan
